# Sanzio Design Template

When designing or redesigning **public / marketing website pages**, treat this folder as the design source of truth:

`C:\Users\Razib\Downloads\Sanzio website\Sanzio website`

## What to follow

- **Layout, typography, spacing, section order, and visual language** from:
  - `Sanzio Homepage (Standalone) (1).html`
- **Images / logos / screenshots / icons** only from:
  - `C:\Users\Razib\Downloads\Sanzio website\Sanzio website\images\`
- Copy needed assets into the frontend public assets folder when implementing (e.g. `public/` or the project’s existing landing image path). Do not invent placeholder stock art when a template image exists.

## Scope

Applies to public pages such as:

- Home, About, Suite/Products, Blog, Connect, Contact
- Files under `src/app/(website)/` and `src/features/landing/`

Does **not** override authenticated dashboard / app UI design unless the user explicitly asks.

## Implementation notes

- Match the template’s composition closely; adapt to existing Next.js/React structure in `oms-v2-frontend`.
- Prefer the template’s brand treatment, hero treatment, and section hierarchy over generic AI landing layouts.
- If template and current code conflict on public pages, prefer the Sanzio template unless the user says otherwise.
